p.src:
Restore the speed of light so that the Newtonian limit is visible: $L_{\mathrm p}
=
-\bigl[mc^2+g\phi(x,t)\bigr]
\sqrt{1-\frac{\dot x^2}{c^2}}.$ For $|\dot x|\ll c$, $\sqrt{1-\frac{\dot x^2}{c^2}}
=
1-\frac{\dot x^2}{2c^2}
+O\!\left(\frac{\dot x^4}{c^4}\right).$ Substitution into  gives $\begin{aligned}
L_{\mathrm p}
&=
-mc^2-g\phi
+\frac{m\dot x^2}{2}
+\frac{g\phi\,\dot x^2}{2c^2}
+O(c^{-4})\\
&\longrightarrow
\frac{m\dot x^2}{2}-g\phi(x,t),
\end{aligned}$ after dropping the constant $-mc^2$ and terms suppressed by $c^{-2}$. The result is the ordinary form $T-V$, so $V_{\mathrm p}(x,t)=g\phi(x,t).$

