p.src:
To expose the source with minimal algebra, place the particle at rest at the origin. The factor $d\tau$ then equals $dt$, and the interaction part of  becomes $S_{\mathrm{int}}
=
-g\int dt\,\phi(\mathbf{0},t).$ This is an integral only along the worldline, whereas  is an integral over all spacetime. To combine them into one spacetime integral, we need a function that selects the particle’s position.

