p.src:
The field Euler–Lagrange equation is $\partial_\mu
\left[
\frac{\partial\mathcal L}
{\partial(\partial_\mu\phi)}
\right]
-
\frac{\partial\mathcal L}{\partial\phi}
=0.$ Applying it to  gives $\boxed{
\partial_t^2\phi-\nabla^2\phi+\mu^2\phi=0
}.$ This is the Klein–Gordon equation. With the mostly-plus convention and $\Box=\partial_\mu\partial^\mu=-\partial_t^2+\nabla^2$, the same equation is $(\Box-\mu^2)\phi=0$.

