p.src:
The particle action now comes back into view: $S_{\mathrm p}
=
-\int d\tau\,
\bigl[m+g\phi(x)\bigr].$ If $\phi$ has a constant background value $\phi_0$, the particle moves as though its mass were $\boxed{
m_{\mathrm{eff}}=m+g\phi_0
}.$ If the bare term $m$ vanishes, the scalar background can provide the entire coefficient multiplying proper time.

